{
  "_comment": "The natural voices the desktop app can download for reading aloud and for Ask ZOOD's answers, in packs: the files one download brings, pinned to one Hugging Face revision, and the voices they speak. Read by src/neural/mod.rs, which keeps a file only once its size and SHA-256 match these (the values Hugging Face publishes, or the digest of the file at that revision for the small ones it keeps in git). Supertonic 3 (Supertone; model OpenRAIL-M, whose use restrictions travel with it; sample code MIT) reads Arabic and English from their letters, every voice in both. Kareem is a Piper voice spoken with the app's own Arabic rules (arabic.rs), not espeak-ng. The first pack is the one offered first.",
